.TH REPOSE 1 "September 2026" "Repose 0.2-dev" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
repose \- sustained C/C++ repository audits
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B repose inventory
.I COMMAND
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.br
.B repose version
.SH DESCRIPTION
Repose builds a reviewable inventory of a fixed repository snapshot, primarily
for KiCad. Use a clean, dedicated scan checkout with a compilation database
configured for that checkout. This release implements inventory building and
review. Model scanning and semantic indexing are upcoming milestones.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B repose inventory build
Save an immutable inventory of HEAD, build inputs, tracked files, and policy.
Identical inputs reuse an existing version. Inherits the current policy and
compilation database path unless explicitly overridden.
.TP
.B repose inventory list
List inventory versions, newest first, with review status.
.TP
.B repose inventory show [ID]
Show an inventory summary. Defaults to current. With --json, export the full
document including files, compilation commands, and policy.
.TP
.B repose inventory files [ID]
List files, defaulting to in-scope code in the current inventory.
.TP
.B repose inventory check [ID]
Validate the checkout commit, tracked cleanliness, and recorded build inputs.
Defaults to current.
.TP
.B repose inventory approve ID
Record review of a specific inventory after validating its checkout and build
inputs. Requires an explicit ID; current and latest are not accepted. Approval does not run
a scan. New inventory versions require their own review.
.TP
.B repose inventory exclude PREFIX... --reason TEXT
Exclude C/C++ files or directory subtrees from direct review. Derive a new
current inventory from the saved map and persist the policy for future builds.
Existing versions stay unchanged. Excluded code remains available as context.
.TP
.B repose inventory include PREFIX... [--reason TEXT]
Restore C/C++ paths to review scope. The new rule overrides previous scope rules
while preserving grouping annotations.
.TP
.B repose inventory exclusions [ID]
List default and explicit scope rules with matched and effective C/C++ counts.
Defaults to current. Effective counts account for later overrides.
.TP
.B repose inventory policy export [ID]
Export the inventory policy as editable JSON. Defaults to current.
.TP
.B repose inventory policy import FILE
Replace the current policy with a JSON policy and derive an inventory version
without accessing source or build files.
.TP
.B repose version
Print the Repose version.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --repo DIR
Dedicated scan checkout, relative to the current directory. Defaults to the
current directory. Available on all inventory commands.
.TP
.B --json
Output JSON. Available on all inventory commands.
.TP
.B --compile-commands FILE
Compilation database for inventory build, relative to the checkout.
Initially defaults to build/compile_commands.json; later builds inherit the
current inventory's compilation database path.
.TP
.B --policy FILE
JSON grouping, exclusion, tag, and note rules for inventory build. Relative to
the current directory. Rules match literal repository-relative prefixes;
a dot matches all paths. Replaces the saved policy on successful build.
Explicit imports reject unmatched rules. Inherited rules for paths absent in a
new snapshot are retained and reported.
.TP
.B --reason TEXT
Reason for a scope decision. Required by exclude; optional for include.
.TP
.B --path PREFIX
Filter inventory files by an exact file or directory prefix.
.TP
.B --group NAME
Filter inventory files by group.
.TP
.B --tag TAG
Filter inventory files by tag.
.TP
.B --status STATUS
Filter inventory files by included, excluded, all, missing-command, or
header-unmapped. Defaults to included. Filters combine by intersection.
.SH INVENTORY IDS
Use a full ID or an unambiguous hexadecimal prefix of at least four characters.
Inventory content is immutable. Rebuilding after changing policy creates a new
version. Approval and timestamps are separate metadata.
Inspection defaults to current, the version selected by the last successful
build or policy edit. The latest selector names the most recently created
version, which can differ after restoring an earlier policy.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I <worktree-git-dir>/repose/repose.sqlite
Worktree-local inventory storage, separate from AIR and other linked worktrees.
.SH LIMITATIONS
Untracked files are outside the source inventory. Generated and external
compilation inputs are counted separately. Headers await semantic association.
The build input checks do not establish freshness of generated headers,
external dependencies, compiler binaries, or an index.
Inspection uses read-only database connections without schema migration.
Writers retain WAL/SHM sidecars for subsequent read-only access. Older databases
without those sidecars require one writable open first.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git (1),
.BR cmake (1),
.BR clangd (1)
